The composite EGI score (d = +0.250, p < 0.001) was superior to using any of the five 
individual components of the EGI measured individually and ranked 10th out of 61 in terms 
of predictive power; this finding indicates that using all five components together into a 
single value provides a stronger and more comprehensive discriminator than any one measure 
alone. 
