4.10 Transformer Attention Map Analysis 
Attention weights were retrieved from both Pre-LN Transformer layers over all 2,416 test 
windows (1,009 PD and 1,407 Control) in order to determine which parts of the 2-second gait 
window the Hybrid CNN-Transformer model prioritized for its judgments. After two 
MaxPool(2) layers in the CNN encoder had reduced the original 200-sample input to 50 
sequence positions (approximately 40 ms gait periods), the geometric mean of Layer 1 and 
Layer 2 attention weights was taken to create a strong fused attention signal.  A temporal 
importance profile was created using the CLS token's attention to signify places 1–50. The 
geometric mean of Layer 1 and Layer 2 attention was utilized to calculate a fused attention, 
