response and mid-stance (0–600 ms, p = 0.6955) and during the initial swing (1200–1600 
ms, p = 0.2409). This is a clinically useful negative finding, these phases are 
biomechanically less impaired in early PD, and the model was able to successfully 
identify them and down-weight the importance of these phases without any phase labels 
or domain supervision, further demonstrating that the attention pattern is an authentic 
reflection of pathological gait knowledge, and not simply signal properties.  
