Analysis: (Table 4.15) 
● The most impressive AUC (0.921) was reported by Nanayakkara et al. [2] who used 
logistic regression on a small sample of CoP features from pressure insoles on a 
significantly smaller sample (39 PD + 38 HC), a different sensor type, and a single 
80/20 split. The proposed Hybrid CNN-Transformer achieved an AUC of 0.8544, a 
more conservative, replicable and clinically generalizable estimate under strict, Group 
5-fold subject level cross-validation (68 PD + 82 HC). 
● The accuracy of 98.6% and the sensitivity of 99.2% reported by Mostafavi et al. [3] 
are considered as suspicious, since no cross validation details or dataset composition 
was provided, and results of this scale are rare for a real world binary gait 
classification task. They can be due to training-set evaluation or data leakage. The 
result in the proposed work is a subject level cross-validated estimate with no data 
leakage, by design. 
