Physionet dataset achieved an accuracy of 87.89% with a 10-fold cross validation 
using segment-level CV. This is not directly comparable to the proposed work for 
three reasons: (a) it uses a different dataset (Physionet) and sensor type (VGRF); (b) 
segment-level CV elevates the performance compared to subject-level CV, because 
the same subject may be present in both train and test folds; and (c) the proposed 
work is binary early-stage detection (H and Y 1–2) rather than multi-class H and Y 
staging (H and Y 2–3, moderate-to-severe). The suggested Hybrid CNN-Transformer 
